  THE CORRECT FORMULA:
  D counts pairs of LABELED (tournament, arc) that are in the SAME class
  AND whose reversals are ALSO in the same class.
  D = #{(T1,e1), (T2,e2) : T1 in C, T2 in C, T1_e1 in D, T2_e2 in D, (T1,e1)!=(T2,e2)}
    summed over all (C,D) pairs, divided by... hmm.

  Actually, D = T - 2E where:
  T = total arc-orbits = sum_C #{arc orbits of C}
  2E = 2 * #{distinct (C,D) pairs with some arc orbit from C to D}
  D = #{arc-orbits from C to D} - 2*#{distinct (C,D) edges}
    = sum over edges (C,D) of (#{orbits from C to D} - 1)
    + sum over edges (D,C) of (#{orbits from D to C} - 1)
    + sum_C (#{self-orbits} - 1 if self-orbits > 0, else 0)

  REVISED: D = sum over all (C,D) adjacent pairs of
  (orbits_C_to_D + orbits_D_to_C - 2)
  + sum_C (self_orbits_C if > 0)

